      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "YING Hui-ch'ien 應撝謙 (T. 嗣寅, H. 潛齋), 1615–1683, scholar, was a native of Jên-ho (Hangchow). A licentiate under the Ming regime, he gave up hope of an official career after the change of dynasty, devoting himself to teaching and writing, and gathering about him a large number of students by his presentation of Neo-Confucian philosophy in which he favored the Ch'êng-Chu school (see under Hu Wei).",
          "source": "eccp-3678191",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        },
        {
          "text": "應撝謙，字潛齋，錢塘人。",
